---
/**
 * 404 — "the same empty-state language as the others" (docs/theme/TEMPERED.md
 * §8). The last page on the site still wearing its pre-theme markup: an
 * unstyled <h1> and two sentences of UA-default body text, on a page that a
 * shopper reaches by following a link that went stale.
 *
 * It is built out of the same parts as the PDP's "Product not found." and the
 * cart's "Nothing held yet.": a display-face line, one muted sentence, and a
 * way out. §10 — no apology, and it states only what it knows. The address
 * resolved to nothing; this page does NOT know why, so it does not speculate
 * about products that sold out or pages that moved.
 *
 * No `cartCount` and no `currency`: this page makes no commerce call, and
 * absence is meaningful in both props (see Base.astro) — a bare "Cart" is
 * honest here, "Cart (0)" would not be.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Page not found">
	<div class="empty">
		<h1 class="empty-title">Page not found.</h1>
		{/* Both sentences state what THIS page knows, and it knows exactly one
		    thing: the address resolved to nothing. "Everything else in the shop
		    is where you left it" was the second sentence until a reviewer
		    screenshotted it rendering, in good faith and falsely, over a store
		    whose content tables were gone (issue #140) — this page makes no
		    commerce and no content call, so any sentence about the state of the
		    shop is invented. So is "the shop is still here". The second
		    sentence therefore points AT the ways out rather than vouching for
		    where they lead; if the shop is down too, its own page says so. */}
		<p class="empty-copy">
			Nothing here under that address. Try the shop, or start from the home page.
		</p>
		<div class="ways-out">
			<a class="u-btn u-btn-ghost" href="/products">Browse the shop</a>
			<a class="home" href="/">Go to the home page</a>
		</div>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	/* §8's empty state, and the same block the PDP and the shop page use: an
	   invitation to act, aligned left, with air above and below it rather than
	   a box around it (§2). */
	.empty {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding-block: 2rem;
	}

	/* §3: the display face, narrow. One step down from a page title — this is
	   the line the shopper reads first on an otherwise bare page. */
	.empty-title {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--u-display);
		font-variation-settings: "wdth" 78, "opsz" 32;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1.75rem;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
		line-height: 1;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.empty-copy {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 44ch;
		color: var(--u-mute);
	}

	/* Two ranks, not two buttons: the shop is the offer, the home page is a
	   link. `align-items: center` so the text link sits on the button's optical
	   centre rather than on its baseline. */
	.ways-out {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		padding-top: 0.25rem;
	}
	.home {
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		color: var(--u-mute);
	}
	.home:hover {
		color: var(--u-ink);
	}
</style>
